  "body": "ROADMAP M11.4: the island's 9 hops are the SW-corner piece of every lap whose 24.7 mm lead grazes 20 deg for 22 mm; whole-lead reading drops hops to 1 but breaks the air budget 3.9x. Next: a lead-scoped dependency or a corner landing off the lead. Work held in tmp/island-r6b.patch (LinkLaw::late). Island regions still fall back to named rings.\r\n\r\nDone means: island regions plan on the HSM planner with legal late returns within the air budget, no ring fallback.\r\n\r\nSource: ROADMAP.md M11.4; RECOMMENDED.md \"M11.4 C round 6\"\r\n",
